    {
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50411036",
      "title": "Ask HN: LLM-Resistant Publishing Strategies",
      "source": "hackernews",
      "sourceName": "Hacker News",
      "summary": "As has been discussed at length, LLM companies carried out the most egregious theft of labor [0] and intellectual property [1] in human history.<p>I am one among the many (artists, musicians, writers, developers), who continue to be appaled at tech billionaires profiting from this [2]. As such, I have mostly ceased publishing original content online, while I wait for effective defenses to emerge.<p>The two industry-standards are `robots.txt` and captchas. Neither works: the former is simply ignored, even by industry heavyweights [3]; the latter is trivial to bypass (using AI itself [4], remote solving services [5], or anti-detect browsers&#x2F;impersonators [6] + residential proxies [7]).<p>Emerging strategies include special fonts for creating OCR-resistant documents, tho current options don&#x27;t seem to be effective [8]. Under the &quot;dark forest&quot; theory [9], paywalling or private distribution seem viable options, provided you can trust the recipients to not leak the content; of course, this is a death sentence for the libre ethos of the past 50 years, tho perhaps it was long overdue [10].<p>Please share your thoughts on any alternatives, real or speculative.<p>[0] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49752056 - Microsoft exec called AI scraping &#x27;the largest theft of labor in human history&#x27; (techcrunch.com)<p>[1] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=41275073 - Ex-Google CEO: AI startups can steal IP and hire lawyers to &#x27;clean up the mess&#x27; (theverge.com)<p>[2] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=40297027 - StackOverflow is banning accounts that delete answers in protest against OpenAI (benui.ca)<p>[3] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=50401213 - Brave Sells Its Search Index to AI, and Your Website Is Probably in It (searchenginejournal.com)<p>[4] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49930138 - Meta&#x27;s Muse is fantastic for web scraping (sigh.dev)<p>[5] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;captchathecat.com&#x2F;<p>[6] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=42547820 - Curl-Impersonate (github.com&#x2F;lexiforest)<p>[7] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=48864252 - An update on residential proxies and the scraper situation (lwn.net)<p>[8] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=48873513 - Ghost Font: A font that humans can read but AI cannot (mixfont.com)<p>[9] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=47566442 - The Cognitive Dark Forest (ryelang.org)<p>[10] https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=50224074 - PHP Foundation &#x27;under-funded&#x27; with one full-time staff member, director says (reuters.com)",
